OldGitFloor findings - kama round-23 build wave
Scope: fail-closed behaviour of global --no-lazy-fetch and --no-replace-objects on git older than 2.44.
Frozen base for comparison: master 4fe9339f. Its tools/report-landing-audit.py has no GIT_ISOLATION and
contains neither flag (git cat-file -p 4fe9339f:tools/report-landing-audit.py | grep: no match).

== 1. Results ==
R1. --no-lazy-fetch does NOT exist before git 2.45.0. The floor is 2.45.0, not 2.44.
    git 2.24.1, 2.43.2 and 2.44.0 refuse it at global position: exit 129, stderr
    "unknown option: --no-lazy-fetch" + usage, empty stdout, and the repo-configured
    promisor command is NOT executed (marker absent). git 2.45.0 and 2.56.0 accept it.
R2. Fail-closed: yes, by refusal. Nothing is evaluated and nothing executes.
R3. --no-replace-objects is accepted and honored on every tested binary, 2.24.1 through 2.56.0.
    It is not a floor-raiser. Documented since git.txt v1.7.0 (absent at v1.6.5).
R4. The env form GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1 is NOT fail-closed below 2.45: it is silently ignored on
    2.43.2 and 2.44.0 (repo command runs; exit 0 "missing") and on 2.24.1 (repo command runs; exit 128).
    It is honored on 2.45.0 and 2.56.0 only. Never use it as a fallback for older git.
R5. Consumer (lane working copy tools/report-landing-audit.py, sha256 79d9e124e8171b47dc69f5af657bcf938fcb77a4915f7758d50eccd6c72f226c):
    on git 2.43.2 the first git call (rev-parse --show-object-format) fails rc=129, the tool
    exits 2 with "could-not-evaluate: git rev-parse --show-object-format in .../lane: rc=129
    unknown option: --no-lazy-fetch", stdout 0 bytes. The same run under host git 2.56.0
    passes that call and fails later only because the trivial fixture has no report file.
    The difference is caused by the flag. GIT_ISOLATION (lines 91-95) is passed to every
    git() call (line 113), so on git <2.45.0 any run that reaches git() is refused as a typed EvalError at its first call.

